00:28:08.764 --> 00:28:10.930
And now this is the cool
part of the business, which

00:28:10.930 --> 00:28:13.000
is completely changing
the way they operate

00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:17.180
and the way they move forward
in the business moving forward.

00:28:17.180 --> 00:28:19.930
So the next one that I wanted
to talk about from there,

00:28:19.930 --> 00:28:20.430
since that--

00:28:20.430 --> 00:28:22.804
I know I've talked about food,
and all of you are hungry,

00:28:22.804 --> 00:28:24.945
I guess, or had your lunch.

00:28:24.945 --> 00:28:26.320
The next one I
want to talk about

00:28:26.320 --> 00:28:30.280
is really about creating
safe and secure society.

00:28:30.280 --> 00:28:33.670
And this is really
happening now, you know?

00:28:33.670 --> 00:28:37.060
What you're seeing here is
from the city of Singapore.

00:28:37.060 --> 00:28:40.180
And they have an initiative
called Safe City.

00:28:40.180 --> 00:28:42.820
And we had an opportunity
of partnering with them

00:28:42.820 --> 00:28:45.160
to really look at all
non-structured data that

00:28:45.160 --> 00:28:48.550
is coming in from video
recordings, that is coming

00:28:48.550 --> 00:28:51.550
in from all the natural
text information, web chat

00:28:51.550 --> 00:28:54.130
information, social
media information.

00:28:54.130 --> 00:28:57.130
Looking at all the traffic
signals and traffic patterns,

00:28:57.130 --> 00:29:00.910
and how to create a command
center, an AI-driven command

00:29:00.910 --> 00:29:05.290
center that will help the
government to monitor cloud

00:29:05.290 --> 00:29:08.630
movements across the cities.

00:29:08.630 --> 00:29:11.050
Understanding and
predicting how the cloud

00:29:11.050 --> 00:29:13.720
behavior is going to look
like on a particular day

00:29:13.720 --> 00:29:14.930
of the week.

00:29:14.930 --> 00:29:17.380
On a particular big
event day or a game day,

00:29:17.380 --> 00:29:18.700
how does it look like?

00:29:18.700 --> 00:29:21.130
And based on that
understanding, how

00:29:21.130 --> 00:29:24.430
can we optimize the whole
setting of the city right

00:29:24.430 --> 00:29:26.980
from traffic
management to taking

00:29:26.980 --> 00:29:28.930
care of any kind of emergency?

00:29:28.930 --> 00:29:31.210
You know, prevention,
how many resources

00:29:31.210 --> 00:29:33.310
we need to apportion
for taking care

00:29:33.310 --> 00:29:36.270
of any kind of risks that might
happen, so on, and so forth.

00:29:36.270 --> 00:29:38.380
You know, that's kind
of a new capability

00:29:38.380 --> 00:29:39.940
that has been developed.

00:29:39.940 --> 00:29:42.160
What it also does is--

00:29:42.160 --> 00:29:45.130
not just looking at predicting
cloud behavior, but also

00:29:45.130 --> 00:29:47.740
anticipate what
kind of incidents

00:29:47.740 --> 00:29:50.020
can happen that
might have a security

00:29:50.020 --> 00:29:52.570
threat or any kind of risk.

00:29:52.570 --> 00:29:54.850
And how do you actually
predict those in advance

00:29:54.850 --> 00:29:58.210
and then prepare for those
kind of events in advance,

00:29:58.210 --> 00:30:01.540
so that you are not
taken by surprise?

00:30:01.540 --> 00:30:05.470
When you look at this example,
it's not about-- just about

00:30:05.470 --> 00:30:08.500
how we are industrializing
and scaling this capability,

00:30:08.500 --> 00:30:10.690
but it's also about
a new capability

00:30:10.690 --> 00:30:12.890
that is just not possible
with human beings,

00:30:12.890 --> 00:30:14.530
and how we are
helping human beings.

00:30:14.530 --> 00:30:16.450
And one of the example is--

00:30:16.450 --> 00:30:18.640
for example, there's
a game day going on,

00:30:18.640 --> 00:30:21.640
and thousands of people like
us, we go into the game you

00:30:21.640 --> 00:30:22.850
into the stadium.

00:30:22.850 --> 00:30:26.740
One person went with a backpack,
and then after two hours

00:30:26.740 --> 00:30:28.900
comes out without the backpack.

00:30:28.900 --> 00:30:32.260
The human being is just
not going to make that out.

00:30:32.260 --> 00:30:35.220
But the machine realizes
that and gives an alert.

00:30:35.220 --> 00:30:36.640
This is a simple example, right?

00:30:36.640 --> 00:30:39.745
And obviously, it has to be done
in a way that it's responsible,

00:30:39.745 --> 00:30:42.410
it takes care of
privacy, and so forth.

00:30:42.410 --> 00:30:44.080
But this is a completely
new capability

00:30:44.080 --> 00:30:46.480
that, if you can scale,
is going to create

00:30:46.480 --> 00:30:48.460
a more safe and
secure environment

00:30:48.460 --> 00:30:49.780
for the entire city.

00:30:49.780 --> 00:30:52.060
And you can scale it
across multiple cities.

00:30:52.060 --> 00:30:55.030
I mean, in the country that
I'm coming from in India,

00:30:55.030 --> 00:30:56.620
our new government,
new minister,

00:30:56.620 --> 00:30:59.350
there's a big initiative
around digital cities.

00:30:59.350 --> 00:31:00.880
You know, there
are 100 cities that

00:31:00.880 --> 00:31:04.970
are getting digitalized and
using this Smart City concept.

00:31:04.970 --> 00:31:07.690
And the advantage of AI
is that you can actually

00:31:07.690 --> 00:31:09.310
scale this pretty fast.

00:31:09.310 --> 00:31:10.960
Once you have
proven the success,

00:31:10.960 --> 00:31:12.520
you can then
replicate that model

00:31:12.520 --> 00:31:15.790
pretty quickly across
the other cities.

00:31:15.790 --> 00:31:17.740
And that, I think,
is a huge, huge power

00:31:17.740 --> 00:31:20.470
that impacts all of us.

00:31:20.470 --> 00:31:23.140
The third example that
I wanted to share,

00:31:23.140 --> 00:31:26.340
this is something we are
playing to ourselves.

00:31:26.340 --> 00:31:29.430
I think Al alluded to that.

00:31:29.430 --> 00:31:32.470
We at Accenture, we run--

00:31:32.470 --> 00:31:34.120
apart from the work
that we do in terms

00:31:34.120 --> 00:31:36.970
of developing the
strategy for our clients,

00:31:36.970 --> 00:31:39.890
executing that strategy
through technology deployment,

00:31:39.890 --> 00:31:42.410
re-imagining the whole
digital transformation.

00:31:42.410 --> 00:31:45.470
And then finally, we help our
clients manage the operations,

00:31:45.470 --> 00:31:46.540
you know?

00:31:46.540 --> 00:31:48.820
And this is a big
business for Accenture.

00:31:48.820 --> 00:31:52.450
And as we speak, over the
last two to three years,

00:31:52.450 --> 00:31:55.300
we are transforming ourselves.

00:31:55.300 --> 00:31:58.330
We are re-imagining how
we manage the business

00:31:58.330 --> 00:32:00.700
processes of our client.

00:32:00.700 --> 00:32:04.690
And we are applying
AI at the core of it.

00:32:04.690 --> 00:32:07.030
Two, three key dimensions.

00:32:07.030 --> 00:32:09.060
One of that is obviously
to take cost out.

00:32:09.060 --> 00:32:11.910
But the bigger purpose
is, how do we actually

00:32:11.910 --> 00:32:13.440
enable our associates?

00:32:13.440 --> 00:32:16.410
You know, we have 100,000
associates working

00:32:16.410 --> 00:32:17.850
in that part of the business.

00:32:17.850 --> 00:32:19.830
How we enable those
associates to do

00:32:19.830 --> 00:32:21.720
much higher value added work?

00:32:21.720 --> 00:32:23.910
How we enable managing
those processes

00:32:23.910 --> 00:32:27.090
in a completely new way
that is powered by AI

00:32:27.090 --> 00:32:29.010
so that it's more accurate?

00:32:29.010 --> 00:32:31.740
You know, it's compliance-ready.

00:32:31.740 --> 00:32:34.500
It's helping us to manage
any kind of fraud that

00:32:34.500 --> 00:32:35.460
might be happening.

00:32:35.460 --> 00:32:38.370
It enables us to manage
better customer relationships

00:32:38.370 --> 00:32:40.060
and supply relationships.

00:32:40.060 --> 00:32:41.520
And that's really
the core purpose,

00:32:41.520 --> 00:32:45.120
you know, as to why we are
re-imagining our own business

00:32:45.120 --> 00:32:47.880
process, business operations
with the power of AI.

00:32:47.880 --> 00:32:51.562
The example here I took from
was on invoice management.

00:32:54.070 --> 00:32:58.360
In a year, we work with about
2,000 clients in the space--

00:32:58.360 --> 00:33:02.940
200 clients in this space
with over 70 million invoices

00:33:02.940 --> 00:33:04.200
that goes through Accenture.

00:33:04.200 --> 00:33:08.370
You know, we are responsible for
authenticating those, managing

00:33:08.370 --> 00:33:10.530
those, validating those.

00:33:10.530 --> 00:33:15.840
It was done with over 6,000-plus
full-time-equivalent employees

00:33:15.840 --> 00:33:16.670
who are doing that.

00:33:16.670 --> 00:33:18.540
It was a hugely manual process.

00:33:18.540 --> 00:33:21.360
And we brought in artificial
intelligence and machine

00:33:21.360 --> 00:33:24.250
learning at the core
of it that completely

00:33:24.250 --> 00:33:26.331
re-imagined this process.

00:33:26.331 --> 00:33:28.830
What we are doing here-- and
we're working very closely with

00:33:28.830 --> 00:33:32.580
Google in driving this, where
we are using basically Google

00:33:32.580 --> 00:33:34.800
Vision API, which is
really a powerful,

00:33:34.800 --> 00:33:38.970
out-of-the-box capability
that is helping us to extract

00:33:38.970 --> 00:33:43.620
the natural text that is there
in the invoice picture along

00:33:43.620 --> 00:33:47.220
with the spatial information
of that particular picture.

00:33:47.220 --> 00:33:49.560
And then bringing that
together, concatenating

00:33:49.560 --> 00:33:52.140
that together to
extract features

00:33:52.140 --> 00:33:53.880
from those concatenations.

00:33:53.880 --> 00:33:56.730
And we created what
we call as basically

00:33:56.730 --> 00:33:58.950
these digitalized
tokens, you know?

00:33:58.950 --> 00:34:01.560
A word with a position,
where it is placed.

00:34:01.560 --> 00:34:03.600
And each of them we are
uniquely identifying

00:34:03.600 --> 00:34:05.250
as digitalize tokens.

00:34:05.250 --> 00:34:07.320
And then we are making
multiple vectors

00:34:07.320 --> 00:34:10.440
around those tokens to
help create features

00:34:10.440 --> 00:34:12.120
that uniquely define that.

00:34:12.120 --> 00:34:13.920
And then those
features are then used

00:34:13.920 --> 00:34:17.699
to train the deep learning
models, which are then fed back

00:34:17.699 --> 00:34:21.179
into the live system
of all the invoices

00:34:21.179 --> 00:34:25.460
that we have to validate that,
to check for issues, errors,

00:34:25.460 --> 00:34:28.199
if there is any kind of
potential fraud or compliance

00:34:28.199 --> 00:34:30.630
issue, and flag
that to the humans.

00:34:30.630 --> 00:34:32.580
And then the human
associate doesn't

00:34:32.580 --> 00:34:35.400
have to do all the grunt work
that was being done earlier,

00:34:35.400 --> 00:34:37.650
but now is more in
an advisory role

00:34:37.650 --> 00:34:39.610
and is more in a
supervisory role,

00:34:39.610 --> 00:34:43.290
whereas all the grunt work
of validating, checking,

00:34:43.290 --> 00:34:45.616
and accuracy, and all of
that is being checked.

00:34:45.616 --> 00:34:47.199
And then there is a
green light given.

00:34:47.199 --> 00:34:48.698
And if there is a
green light given,

00:34:48.698 --> 00:34:52.989
and the human agent has approved
it, it goes on for processing.

00:34:52.989 --> 00:34:55.110
If there are fraud or
compliance-related issues

00:34:55.110 --> 00:34:57.930
or missing information or
some duplicate information,

00:34:57.930 --> 00:35:00.570
some conflicting information,
that's flagged off as well

00:35:00.570 --> 00:35:01.560
to the human agent.

00:35:01.560 --> 00:35:03.060
And then the human
agent accordingly

00:35:03.060 --> 00:35:06.300
takes more supervisory and
advisory kind of function

00:35:06.300 --> 00:35:07.320
from there.

00:35:07.320 --> 00:35:09.300
And the fact that
we are deploying it

00:35:09.300 --> 00:35:11.910
on Google technology
with the Cloud Platform,

00:35:11.910 --> 00:35:15.060
it has really helped us scale
from one client to 200 clients

00:35:15.060 --> 00:35:15.870
today.

00:35:15.870 --> 00:35:19.620
And the fact that we are
managing 70 million invoices

00:35:19.620 --> 00:35:22.200
in a year, it gives us a
huge amount of data sets

00:35:22.200 --> 00:35:24.570
with different form
factors of invoices,

00:35:24.570 --> 00:35:27.840
different kind of text
orientations, and all of that

00:35:27.840 --> 00:35:32.310
to train and make our
intelligent engine much more

00:35:32.310 --> 00:35:34.590
efficient as days go by.

00:35:34.590 --> 00:35:38.100
And we are right now
over 90%, 95% accurate

00:35:38.100 --> 00:35:42.180
in terms of checking the
validations of these invoices.

00:35:42.180 --> 00:35:44.800
So that's a huge impact for us.

00:35:44.800 --> 00:35:48.000
It helps us give better
service to our clients.

00:35:48.000 --> 00:35:50.510
At the same time, creates
a much more foolproof

00:35:50.510 --> 00:35:52.220
for business process system.

00:35:54.820 --> 00:35:56.710
So having talked about
the other examples

00:35:56.710 --> 00:35:58.540
that Al talked
about on consumer,

00:35:58.540 --> 00:36:02.270
you know, we talked about from
how it helps with agriculture,

00:36:02.270 --> 00:36:05.516
whether it's about re-imagining
our own business process,

00:36:05.516 --> 00:36:07.390
I want to kind of spend
time a little bit now

00:36:07.390 --> 00:36:09.316
in terms of how to get it right.

00:36:09.316 --> 00:36:10.940
I mean, all of these
are great stories.

00:36:10.940 --> 00:36:14.320
We talked about some
of the examples.

00:36:14.320 --> 00:36:18.130
And I want to touch upon three
key tenets or secret sauce

00:36:18.130 --> 00:36:20.720
that we are seeing that
is very important to get

00:36:20.720 --> 00:36:22.834
the intelligent
enterprise journey right.

00:36:22.834 --> 00:36:24.250
The first and
foremost that we are

00:36:24.250 --> 00:36:26.410
seeing with clients who
are very successful in this

00:36:26.410 --> 00:36:30.250
is really figuring out the
human-machine collaboration.

00:36:30.250 --> 00:36:33.370
You know, this is the first
C. The collaboration C.

00:36:33.370 --> 00:36:35.530
This is extremely important,
because human beings

00:36:35.530 --> 00:36:38.030
have certain strengths around
creativity, decision making,

00:36:38.030 --> 00:36:41.060
judgment, whereas the
machines have strength really

00:36:41.060 --> 00:36:42.910
around doing things in
a repeatable manner.

00:36:42.910 --> 00:36:45.310
High accuracy,
high speed, right?

00:36:45.310 --> 00:36:47.800
How do we bring that
together and design

00:36:47.800 --> 00:36:52.570
systems, AI systems that really
take care of these two angles

00:36:52.570 --> 00:36:53.290
very well?

00:36:53.290 --> 00:36:55.150
This is going to be
very, very important.

00:36:55.150 --> 00:36:57.580
It is going to address
the fact whether humans

00:36:57.580 --> 00:36:58.540
are going to compete.

00:36:58.540 --> 00:36:59.290
Absolutely no.

00:36:59.290 --> 00:37:01.780
Humans are going to work
together with machines

00:37:01.780 --> 00:37:03.580
powered by these AI systems.

00:37:03.580 --> 00:37:05.440
And you can think
of it almost as

00:37:05.440 --> 00:37:09.130
if human ingenuity is
actually getting complemented

00:37:09.130 --> 00:37:10.660
with intelligent technology.

00:37:10.660 --> 00:37:14.690
And organizations need to really
figure this out very well.

00:37:14.690 --> 00:37:16.620
And this is not just
a technology play.

00:37:16.620 --> 00:37:19.420
It is about re-imagining
the whole persona

00:37:19.420 --> 00:37:21.420
as to who is going
to use that system,

00:37:21.420 --> 00:37:24.610
you know, whether it's that
agricultural farmer, whether it

00:37:24.610 --> 00:37:28.360
is the customer, value manager,
or a marketing manager,

00:37:28.360 --> 00:37:30.430
whether it's the supply
chain manager, whether it

00:37:30.430 --> 00:37:32.470
is the event manager.

00:37:32.470 --> 00:37:33.970
Who is going to
use the AI system

00:37:33.970 --> 00:37:37.630
and how he or she can
then work with the machine

00:37:37.630 --> 00:37:39.880
to actually create a
much higher performance,

00:37:39.880 --> 00:37:41.050
much higher outcome?

00:37:41.050 --> 00:37:46.840
And keeping that design thinking
in mind when you develop the AI

00:37:46.840 --> 00:37:48.550
system is extremely critical.

00:37:48.550 --> 00:37:50.330
So that's the first C.

00:37:50.330 --> 00:37:53.740
The second big focus is
really around capabilities

00:37:53.740 --> 00:37:55.860
and capabilities
that are end-to-end.

00:37:55.860 --> 00:37:58.660
And I wanted to touch upon
this, because people sometimes

00:37:58.660 --> 00:38:01.660
feel that capabilities means
technology, which we have all

00:38:01.660 --> 00:38:05.020
talked about so far, all
the different algorithms,

00:38:05.020 --> 00:38:06.460
the machine learning
capabilities.

00:38:06.460 --> 00:38:09.550
Yes, that is great, but
that's just one part

00:38:09.550 --> 00:38:11.020
of the capability.

00:38:11.020 --> 00:38:13.510
The second big part of the
capability that is required

00:38:13.510 --> 00:38:16.060
is the fuel for the
whole AI system.

00:38:16.060 --> 00:38:17.140
That's the data.

00:38:17.140 --> 00:38:18.380
That's the data platform.

00:38:18.380 --> 00:38:21.190
How do you get your data
supply chain in place?

00:38:21.190 --> 00:38:25.140
Because that's going to be the
concrete asset on top of which

00:38:25.140 --> 00:38:28.070
you will be actually building
all of these AI systems.

00:38:28.070 --> 00:38:31.600
It's also about how do
you then embed the AI

00:38:31.600 --> 00:38:33.640
system into your
business functions,

00:38:33.640 --> 00:38:35.320
into your business processes?

00:38:35.320 --> 00:38:38.570
And that requires a different
skill, different capability

00:38:38.570 --> 00:38:41.270
on adoption, around
change management,

00:38:41.270 --> 00:38:43.900
around making sure that
employees are really

00:38:43.900 --> 00:38:44.785
believing in it.

00:38:44.785 --> 00:38:47.720
And there is a tangible
value for the employees

00:38:47.720 --> 00:38:49.460
in the organization.

00:38:49.460 --> 00:38:53.260
And how do you bring all of
these end-to-end capabilities

00:38:53.260 --> 00:38:57.100
right from having a strategy
of AI to actually creating

00:38:57.100 --> 00:39:00.370
the platform, enabling all of
these different capabilities

00:39:00.370 --> 00:39:01.850
that we spoke about earlier?

00:39:01.850 --> 00:39:04.510
And then how do you manage
the change and the adoption

00:39:04.510 --> 00:39:05.770
into the business?

00:39:05.770 --> 00:39:09.324
That creates real
transformation.

00:39:09.324 --> 00:39:10.740
And then the third
one that I want

00:39:10.740 --> 00:39:14.060
to speak about is as you
think of these capabilities,

00:39:14.060 --> 00:39:16.060
how do you go about
building those?

00:39:16.060 --> 00:39:18.940
And that's where the third
C, which is the connections,

00:39:18.940 --> 00:39:20.562
is extremely important.

00:39:20.562 --> 00:39:21.520
And we are seeing that.

00:39:21.520 --> 00:39:24.400
And we did a big research
on this last year

00:39:24.400 --> 00:39:27.130
around how to increase the
artificial intelligence

00:39:27.130 --> 00:39:29.620
quotient of organizations.

00:39:29.620 --> 00:39:32.110
And we saw that
the companies which

00:39:32.110 --> 00:39:34.570
are taking an outside-in
approach-- by that,

00:39:34.570 --> 00:39:37.400
I mean taking an approach
of bringing innovation,

00:39:37.400 --> 00:39:41.260
not just from within, but from
outside, working with startups,

00:39:41.260 --> 00:39:43.780
working with
research institutes,

00:39:43.780 --> 00:39:45.580
working with academia.

00:39:45.580 --> 00:39:48.970
They get a boost start
compared to the companies

00:39:48.970 --> 00:39:50.890
which are trying to do
everything in-house.

00:39:50.890 --> 00:39:54.504
So a critical decision factor
that every leading organization

00:39:54.504 --> 00:39:56.170
in the AI space will
have to think about

00:39:56.170 --> 00:39:58.780
is what they build
on their own, what

00:39:58.780 --> 00:40:02.440
is it that they want to buy
from a service provider,

00:40:02.440 --> 00:40:04.300
and what is it that
they borrow, what is it

00:40:04.300 --> 00:40:05.883
that they get inspired
with, you know,

00:40:05.883 --> 00:40:09.070
using the power of startups or
the academia or the research

00:40:09.070 --> 00:40:10.000
partners.

00:40:10.000 --> 00:40:12.010
And I think that
partnership ecosystem

00:40:12.010 --> 00:40:14.020
is going to be extremely
critical, especially

00:40:14.020 --> 00:40:18.410
as we scale the AI agenda
within the companies.

00:40:18.410 --> 00:40:20.230
So having spoken
about that, I want

00:40:20.230 --> 00:40:21.880
to leave with this
last thought is

00:40:21.880 --> 00:40:25.810
that as we think of
re-imagining the business,

00:40:25.810 --> 00:40:28.630
as we think about creating
the transformation,

00:40:28.630 --> 00:40:31.270
we have to do it in a
very responsible way.

00:40:31.270 --> 00:40:33.350
AI is a profound technology.

00:40:33.350 --> 00:40:35.750
It has a huge value potential.

00:40:35.750 --> 00:40:37.630
But how do we make
sure that there

00:40:37.630 --> 00:40:40.450
is a certain level of
accountability that

00:40:40.450 --> 00:40:43.100
comes in when we are
deploying AI systems?

00:40:43.100 --> 00:40:45.460
How do we make sure that
organizations are thinking

00:40:45.460 --> 00:40:47.080
about every stakeholder?

00:40:47.080 --> 00:40:48.970
Not just the customer,
not just the supplier.

00:40:48.970 --> 00:40:51.700
The employees, the
government, the policy makers,

00:40:51.700 --> 00:40:54.310
how we think of all of
those stakeholders, right?

00:40:54.310 --> 00:40:57.870
And how do we create a right
amount of governance model

00:40:57.870 --> 00:40:59.740
and operating model to see--

00:40:59.740 --> 00:41:02.650
as decisions are being
taken by AI systems,

00:41:02.650 --> 00:41:04.210
who takes the accountability?

00:41:04.210 --> 00:41:06.620
Whether it is the algorithm
which is accountable,

00:41:06.620 --> 00:41:08.800
whether it is the person
who made the algorithm is

00:41:08.800 --> 00:41:11.170
accountable, whether the
person who is actually

00:41:11.170 --> 00:41:13.480
the sponsor of this
whole initiative--

00:41:13.480 --> 00:41:14.879
who are accountable for that?

00:41:14.879 --> 00:41:17.170
And these are questions that
needs to be really thought

00:41:17.170 --> 00:41:19.210
through very, very carefully.

00:41:19.210 --> 00:41:21.400
And as you go through
that transformation,

00:41:21.400 --> 00:41:22.685
think about the people.

00:41:22.685 --> 00:41:25.060
Think about the people that
need to be the rescaled, that

00:41:25.060 --> 00:41:27.820
needs to be rotated
into the new AI journey

00:41:27.820 --> 00:41:30.790
so that we don't leave anybody
as we go into the journey.

00:41:30.790 --> 00:41:33.349
How do we take the people
who probably are not skilled,

00:41:33.349 --> 00:41:35.140
who really don't
understand and appreciate,

00:41:35.140 --> 00:41:36.470
how do we educate them?

00:41:36.470 --> 00:41:39.220
How do we make them the
advocates of the AI journey?

00:41:39.220 --> 00:41:41.050
And more importantly,
how do we make

00:41:41.050 --> 00:41:44.800
them successful in their career
and in their journey with AI?

00:41:44.800 --> 00:41:47.030
And last, but not
the least, security.

00:41:47.030 --> 00:41:48.640
How do we make it
all very secure,

00:41:48.640 --> 00:41:51.100
so that there is no bug
that comes into the AI

00:41:51.100 --> 00:41:53.860
algorithm, which is running
a manufacturing operations

00:41:53.860 --> 00:41:55.109
or a customer operations?

00:41:55.109 --> 00:41:56.650
Because there is a
lot of liquidation

00:41:56.650 --> 00:41:58.600
risk associated with that.

00:41:58.600 --> 00:42:02.980
How do we manage that in
a very responsible manner?

00:42:02.980 --> 00:42:06.820
So with that, I would like
to bring it to a close here.

00:42:06.820 --> 00:42:09.550
Personally, being in the
practice for so many years,

00:42:09.550 --> 00:42:12.920
I feel this is an amazing field.

00:42:12.920 --> 00:42:14.980
A few things I want
us to remember--

00:42:14.980 --> 00:42:18.430
that AI is all about
augmenting human beings.

00:42:18.430 --> 00:42:21.820
How do we think about creating,
living adaptable business

00:42:21.820 --> 00:42:22.780
processes?

00:42:22.780 --> 00:42:26.450
And how do really make sure that
we are all becoming data native

00:42:26.450 --> 00:42:29.620
and enabling that new culture
within the organization?

00:42:29.620 --> 00:42:31.469
And as we do that,
how do we make sure

00:42:31.469 --> 00:42:33.010
we do it in a way
that's responsible?

00:42:33.010 --> 00:42:37.836
It creates trust, transparency,
and addresses people's concerns

00:42:37.836 --> 00:42:39.460
and take them together
in that journey.

00:42:39.460 --> 00:42:42.210
[MUSIC PLAYING]

